From 315a7d410105078365889fb04f7812bb73333d3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:06:16 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: camss: csiphy-3ph: add SM8650 C-PHY lane
 settings

Add C-PHY lane settings for the SM8650 CSIPHY (v2.2.0) so the C-PHY
support can be used there. The register values are the 3-phase lane
settings and the data-rate dependent settings for up to 2.5 Gsps and
up to 3.5 Gsps per trio from the Qualcomm camera kernel CSIPHY v2.2.0
table (cam_csiphy_2_2_0_hwreg.h), resolved for a short channel. The
table is chosen from the link frequency (half the symbol rate).

As in that driver, C-PHY uses the vendor settle count (6 ns, 5.8 ns
above 2.5 Gsps, in 200 ps units), common control 7 = 0x7a and releases
the 3-phase reset with common control 0 = 0x0e followed by 3 ms.

Source: Xiaomi aurora-u-oss camera kernel,
https://github.com/MiCode/vendor_qcom_opensource_camera-kernel/blob/34fcdfe570843fb890d4434fd0caf56a00deca97/drivers/cam_sensor_module/cam_csiphy/include/cam_csiphy_2_2_0_hwreg.h

Signed-off-by: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
---
 .../qcom/camss/camss-csiphy-3ph-1-0.c         | 254 +++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 252 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

